id: pm-745epp
title: Suppress inferred test telemetry before identity creation and export
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1243. Inferred test execution does not mint an installation identity queue events spawn workers or export OTLP unless explicitly opted in; explicit source context remains deliberate; disabled telemetry always wins."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-12T21:08:25.575Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T23:48:09.532Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-12T23:48:09.004Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-12T23:48:09.004Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Inferred test execution does not mint an installation identity queue events spawn workers or export OTLP unless explicitly opted in; explicit source context remains deliberate; disabled telemetry always wins.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Suppress inferred test telemetry before identity creation and export
value: Reliable privacy-preserving operational context for agents and package consumers
parent: pm-5oj5
resolution: Shared test consent policy suppresses inferred traffic before identity creation; Sentry remains disabled for present Vitest flags including empty values even when test telemetry is explicit.
expected_result: Inferred tests remain silent by default and intentional telemetry cannot bypass Vitest Sentry isolation.
actual_result: Two empty-flag cases failed before correction and pass afterward; 86 focused tests and all 8791 tests pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage.
